{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' research/ocr-morphology-and-mixed-script-20261003.md && sed -n '1,60p' research/hao-publication-held-for-actual-glyph-20261003.md && rg -n '\\\"key\\\": \\\"ziyuan-2012:597D|虘钟|虘鐘|好.*hào|\\\"2bce4fa87802\\\"' content/entries/597D.json content/dossiers/597D.json research\"","aggregated_output":"/home/catalin/.profile: line 29: /tmp/mfc-uv-bin/env: No such file or directory\n# OCR morphology and mixed-script verification\n\nThe 好 passage at 字源 PDF 1109 / printed 1094 exposes two general failures:\nplausible names biased repeated scan checks, and a multi-character replacement\nnormalized a correctly printed adjacent simplified character. The raw span is\n虐钟; the target first graph has a closed lower component, matching the same\nbook's 虘 headword rather than the open-right lower part of its 虐 headword.\nThe adjacent scan graph is 钟, not 鐘. A proposed 虘鐘 replacement was therefore\nonly partly supported.\n\nNamed checks incorrectly reported raw 虐 even while describing geometry that\ncontradicts its source-raster control. Those receipts are preserved. A genuine\nLuna low higher-resolution blind comparison, with target and randomized source\ncontrols and no character names or OCR verdicts, matched the closed-lower target\nto the 虘 control. The coordinator independently inspected the original target\nand controls. The exact attachments, image hashes and blind review result are\nretained in the 好 source job's `ocr-morphology-blind-comparison-highres/` stage.\n\nThe generic occurrence-verification instruction now requires discriminating\npixel geometry before character identification, checks each character of a span,\npreserves mixed scripts, and calls for a genuine retained blind comparison when\nnamed identities bias conflicting reviews. This is not a universal rule about\nancient graph etymology. It does not automatically certify images or modify OCR.\nActual producer overlays and rebuilt consumer verification remain required;\nthis note records the finding, not completion of the producer repair.\n\n## Applied producer and consumer verification\n\nThe producer now repairs only raw offsets [1438,1439), 虐 → 虘. Its actual\n`research_corrections.load_effective(page-1109)` validator passes. Effective\nproducer text at [1438,1440) is 虘钟, and the current consumer record ending\n`:001109` matches that complete effective text exactly. Raw OCR is preserved.\n\n- Decoded source scan: `f57b420e60d20032f8df525c5dcae08228f9a01195720435613d53d0c14df040`.\n- Original OCR evidence: `4ad1c5141bed8484c5d9088ce5888c2293aa5357267fc4ba04554e6f41620b56`.\n- Effective evidence: `83da0aaef5c5f850afd23793440be39bf5847b19a5f1d4cdec8fb68e8d6a6022`.\n\nThe actual blind result is at `ocr-morphology-blind-comparison-highres/result.json`\n(directly in the stage, not a `review/` subdirectory). It explicitly identifies\nthe target's closed right-side geometry and matches `right_control`. The\nproducer's initial receipt path typo was reported for correction. Fresh source\ncontinuation and article reviews remain required; this verification does not\nclaim the 好 article is published or the entire OCR page reviewed.\n# Hold 好 for actual selected-glyph and source evidence repair\n\nThe genuine approved pair a252c6eb… / 9ae81979… was not published. Final root\ninspection of exact asset 7f47359d… PNG found its caption/alt/history still say\nsmall upper figure and larger lower figure, despite the actual image showing a\nmuch larger upper assembly (two enclosed spaces and crosswise stroke) and a\nsmaller angular lower figure with descending stem. Earlier correct curator\ngeometry had been overwritten by later contradictory reviews. Real pass\nreceipts remain preserved as failed substantive evidence, not deleted or faked.\n\nThe book record X-4bbb750063ebdb6f6ce4 also still calls the scanned vessel span\n虘鐘 and says no corpus correction was made. The producer/consumer now actually\nhave first-only 虐→虘, preserving printed 钟. The record must be superseded by\ngenuine corrected scan research, not manually rewritten. The article does not\nname that vessel, but an asserted exact scan reading in supporting provenance\nmust not silently pass as verified.\n\nThe current candidate also generates meaning edges from statements denying an\nestablished development; those belong in limitations under the shared corrected\ncontract. The actual author/curator/research agents are repairing these connected\nfields and obtaining fresh exact-pair reviews and source-resolution receipts.\nNo new issue was opened for these repeat manifestations.\n\nGeneric visual policy now focuses captions on useful visible contrasts and\nrequires explanatory value as well as pixel support for size/stroke details.\nFor 好 the vertical versus horizontal arrangements are useful; an exhaustive\ninvented stroke description is not. Existing selected-glyph checks still apply,\nand this prompt change approves no old article. The contrasting 学 redraw\nprovenance repair likewise retains only visibly and historically supported claims.\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:107:      \"text\": \"The entry analyzes 好 as 女 plus 子 and favors a mother–child affection interpretation because early 子 forms are child-shaped and smaller than 女. It records competing proposals: a beautiful woman (Duan Yucai) and affection between a man and woman (Xu Kai and Chen Weizhan). The entry says early written uses employ extended meanings and do not attest the proposed mother–child affection sense directly. It dates the surname use 婦好 to Shang oracle-bone and bronze material, cites oracle-bone 《合集》154, 婦好娩, and identifies Fu Hao as a Shang military leader. It reports that bronze inscriptions first show the sense ‘good/beautiful’ (虘鐘: 用樂好賓), also ‘friendly’ (杜伯盨: 好朋友), and a phonetic loan for 孝 on 羌伯簋. Warring States bamboo texts attest ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and ‘friendly/peace’ (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Some Warring States bamboo forms use 丑 in place of 女. The page lists one oracle-bone form and 13 of 129 bronze forms; the glyph images were not visually inspected here.\",\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:206:      \"text\": \"The entry reports that bronze inscriptions first show 好 meaning ‘good/beautiful’, citing 虘鐘: 用樂好賓; it also cites 杜伯盨: 好朋友 for ‘friendly’. It gives Warring States bamboo examples for ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and friendly relations (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Its inspected text does not supply absolute dates for the named bronze vessels, so these establish source-attributed inscriptional examples and broad period categories rather than a precisely dated first occurrence.\",\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:457:        \"query\": \"好 hǎo hào Guangyun 呼皓 呼到 Baxter Sagart Zhengzhang\",\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:465:        \"query\": \"好 earliest occurrence Shijing good character bronze inscription 虘鐘 好賓\",\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:508:        \"query\": \"好 商代 甲骨文 婦好 金文 虘鐘 用樂好賓 断代\",\ncontent/dossiers/597D.json:513:        \"outcome\": \"Opened and inspected the CUHK entry and Academia Sinica museum article. The former provides inscription citations and broad period labels; the inspected text does not give an absolute date for the 虘鐘 example.\"\ncontent/entries/597D.json:598:      \"text\": \"The entry analyzes 好 as 女 plus 子 and favors a mother–child affection interpretation because early 子 forms are child-shaped and smaller than 女. It records competing proposals: a beautiful woman (Duan Yucai) and affection between a man and woman (Xu Kai and Chen Weizhan). The entry says early written uses employ extended meanings and do not attest the proposed mother–child affection sense directly. It dates the surname use 婦好 to Shang oracle-bone and bronze material, cites oracle-bone 《合集》154, 婦好娩, and identifies Fu Hao as a Shang military leader. It reports that bronze inscriptions first show the sense ‘good/beautiful’ (虘鐘: 用樂好賓), also ‘friendly’ (杜伯盨: 好朋友), and a phonetic loan for 孝 on 羌伯簋. Warring States bamboo texts attest ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and ‘friendly/peace’ (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Some Warring States bamboo forms use 丑 in place of 女. The page lists one oracle-bone form and 13 of 129 bronze forms; the glyph images were not visually inspected here.\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:697:      \"text\": \"The entry reports that bronze inscriptions first show 好 meaning ‘good/beautiful’, citing 虘鐘: 用樂好賓; it also cites 杜伯盨: 好朋友 for ‘friendly’. It gives Warring States bamboo examples for ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and friendly relations (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Its inspected text does not supply absolute dates for the named bronze vessels, so these establish source-attributed inscriptional examples and broad period categories rather than a precisely dated first occurrence.\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:976:        \"text\": \"The entry analyzes 好 as 女 plus 子 and favors a mother–child affection interpretation because early 子 forms are child-shaped and smaller than 女. It records competing proposals: a beautiful woman (Duan Yucai) and affection between a man and woman (Xu Kai and Chen Weizhan). The entry says early written uses employ extended meanings and do not attest the proposed mother–child affection sense directly. It dates the surname use 婦好 to Shang oracle-bone and bronze material, cites oracle-bone 《合集》154, 婦好娩, and identifies Fu Hao as a Shang military leader. It reports that bronze inscriptions first show the sense ‘good/beautiful’ (虘鐘: 用樂好賓), also ‘friendly’ (杜伯盨: 好朋友), and a phonetic loan for 孝 on 羌伯簋. Warring States bamboo texts attest ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and ‘friendly/peace’ (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Some Warring States bamboo forms use 丑 in place of 女. The page lists one oracle-bone form and 13 of 129 bronze forms; the glyph images were not visually inspected here.\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:1075:        \"text\": \"The entry reports that bronze inscriptions first show 好 meaning ‘good/beautiful’, citing 虘鐘: 用樂好賓; it also cites 杜伯盨: 好朋友 for ‘friendly’. It gives Warring States bamboo examples for ‘like’ (郭店《老子甲》32) and friendly relations (清華簡《繫年》39, 108). Its inspected text does not supply absolute dates for the named bronze vessels, so these establish source-attributed inscriptional examples and broad period categories rather than a precisely dated first occurrence.\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:1326:          \"query\": \"好 hǎo hào Guangyun 呼皓 呼到 Baxter Sagart Zhengzhang\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:1334:          \"query\": \"好 earliest occurrence Shijing good character bronze inscription 虘鐘 好賓\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:1377:          \"query\": \"好 商代 甲骨文 婦好 金文 虘鐘 用樂好賓 断代\",\ncontent/entries/597D.json:1382:          \"outcome\": \"Opened and inspected the CUHK entry and Academia Sinica museum article. The former provides inscription citations and broad period labels; the inspected text does not give an absolute date for the 虘鐘 example.\"\nresearch/ocr-morphology-and-mixed-script-20261003.md:8:The adjacent scan graph is 钟, not 鐘. A proposed 虘鐘 replacement was therefore\nresearch/ocr-morphology-and-mixed-script-20261003.md:31:producer text at [1438,1440) is 虘钟, and the current consumer record ending\nresearch/hao-publication-held-for-actual-glyph-20261003.md:12:虘鐘 and says no corpus correction was made. The producer/consumer now actually\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
